<title>GERMANY: End pointless EMU debate - German CDU.</title>
<headline>End pointless EMU debate - German CDU.</headline>
<dateline>LEIPZIG, Germany 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German political leaders should put a stop to the pointless debate over the introduction of the euro, said Bernhard Vogel, Christian Democrat (CDU) premier of the east German state of Thuringia.</p>
<p>&quot;We should put the discussion to rest and make sure that the citizens and the economy get ready,&quot; said Vogel in an interview with the Leipziger Zeitung newspaper.</p>
<p>Both a softening of the convergence criteria and a delay of the January 1999 start date would be damaging for Germany, politically and economically. Any delay could scupper the project forever, he said.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
